WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.300
Build capacity nearly doubled.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.100
Accepted outcomes did not.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.566
This is Leverage Lab.

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:08.233
It is a small simulator that shows why.

00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:12.866
Work moves through six stages, from shape to adopt.

00:00:12.866 --> 00:00:16.666
Work counts only when people use it and someone owns it.

00:00:16.666 --> 00:00:20.733
Each stage can pass a limited amount of good work each week.

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:22.800
Build can pass about 19 items.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.466
Verify can pass about 5.

00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:24.600
7.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.666
So Verify sets the pace for the whole system.

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:30.466
But you cannot see that.

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:35.000
Telemetry shows 95 percent of Build, and only 32 percent of Verify.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.400
Build has the biggest queue and the most activity.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.466
So the evidence points at Build, with 71 percent confidence.

00:00:42.466 --> 00:00:46.133
The loudest stage is not the stage that limits output.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.466
Suppose you trust that evidence.

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:53.266
Every cycle, you add more agents and a delivery partner.

00:00:53.266 --> 00:00:57.133
Over four six-week cycles, accepted outcomes fall from 5.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:57.600
2 to 1.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.333
3 per week.

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:01.333
Work in progress grows from 64 items to 148.

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.800
More building made the system worse.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.200
Now spend at the real constraint.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.933
In cycle one, automate verification and limit new work.

00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:12.200
Output rises to 6.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.266
5 per week, and the constraint moves to Adopt.

00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:18.800
In cycle two, fund adoption and make handoffs clear.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.666
Output reaches 10 per week.

00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:23.400
And the constraint moves back to Verify.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.066
Then you repeat the plan that worked.

00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:28.333
Output falls to 4.

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:29.466
2, and then to 3.

00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:29.600
7.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:35.000
The constraint moved, and the repeated limit on new work now starves the system.

00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:37.633
The constraint moves.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:39.900
Find it again after every change.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.766
Try it yourself in the lab.
